{"version":"1","id":"codimis","handle":"codimis","name":"Codimis","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/7c16560c41b94e4888cb7870aec70c21","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-8.2806,"y":7.0929,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":53,"newest_post_at":"2024-03-22T11:35:45.094Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-08-24T08:46:55.918Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.132075,"avg_read_time":3.754717,"summary_length_avg":323.377358,"title_length_avg":48.811321,"title_length_var":285.813457,"tag_entropy":2.650895,"tag_diversity":0.660377,"top_tag_share":0.641509,"avg_upvotes":7.283019,"median_upvotes":5.0,"avg_comments":0.679245,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.095607,"zero_engagement_share":0.0,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.871237,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.622642,"recency_skew":0.65625},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[6.1324,7.9853],"cadence_depth":[-4.1471,-5.1765],"hype_variety":[-6.8088,-5.25],"title_style":[9.2353,-7.3971]},"top_tags":[["java",39],["interview-questions",8],["flutter",8],["performance",5],["interview",4],["android",3],["database",2],["gradle",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["The Best Guide to Enhance Your Terminal Experience and Productivity with Zsh and Fig","How to Build a Spring Boot REST API with Java\u00a0?","Code First or Database First\u00a0?"],"outlier":["The String Concatenation Trap: Why You Should Avoid It in Loops and How to Fix It"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"kbtKMbD8m","title":"What is Server Sent Event(SSE) and How to Use It in Java Spring Boot?","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/what-is-server-sent-event-sse-and-how-to-use-it-in-java-spring-boot-7f4ffa828882?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-server-sent-event-sse-and-how-to-use-it-in-java-spring-boot--kbtkmbd8m","summary":"SSE is a technology for transmitting data from a server to a web client in real-time. It allows the client to establish a persistent connection to the server and receive updates without sending frequent requests. SSE is widely used in applications such as chat apps, stock tickers, and social media feeds. In a Java Spring Boot application, SSE can be implemented using the `javax.servlet.AsyncContext` and the `EventSource` object in JavaScript.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c1e1461bf593949f352802146d997034?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-22T11:35:45.094Z"},{"id":"QrMrIBANC","title":"Performance-based animation and animation example in Flutter","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/performance-based-animation-and-animation-example-in-flutter-2b4affaa5375?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/performance-based-animation-and-animation-example-in-flutter-qrmribanc","summary":"This post explains how to use animations efficiently in Flutter and the concept of 'Shader compilation jank'. It also provides examples of creating different animations using Flutter.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/911fe02fa0d42277b9ee3629dafc5915?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-22T11:18:23.663Z"},{"id":"kqyX7q0HW","title":"Code First or Database First\u00a0?","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/code-first-or-database-first-222523a195bf?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/code-first-or-database-first--kqyx7q0hw","summary":"Code First and Database First are two approaches to setting up an Entity Framework data model. Code First involves defining the model using C# or VB.NET classes and using Entity Framework's migration features to update the database schema. Database First involves creating a database first and then generating the entity classes with Entity Framework.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9b039cbd4ce615f1e758a2a743871afd?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":17,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-03-22T11:17:43.692Z"},{"id":"HYBAHAiEw","title":"Literals in Java: Why New Keywords Aren't Needed for Expressive Code","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/understanding-literals-in-java-80133b81f225?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/literals-in-java-why-new-keywords-aren-t-needed-for-expressive-code-hybahaiew","summary":"Literals in Java are constants that represent fixed values in code. They include numeric literals, character and string literals, boolean literals, and null literals. The use of literals in Java enhances code readability, expressiveness, and efficiency. The 'new' keyword is not needed for literals because they are immutable and constant, and the Java compiler optimizes their usage through the constant pool.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/cb271ed1e0d1130a0983b5187e209c22?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-06T07:36:00.772Z"},{"id":"PEHbrsQBO","title":"Effective Java Coding Practices","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/effective-java-coding-practices-55d0b776f503?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/effective-java-coding-practices-pehbrsqbo","summary":"Learn effective Java coding practices, including using descriptive names, following naming conventions, formatting code consistently, and more.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d230bde69d785725f982918eb321f0a1?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":14,"created_at":"2023-11-03T09:48:38.767Z"},{"id":"1tOSzbkS0","title":"Default Values of Primitive Types in Java","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/default-values-of-primitive-types-in-java-aa26ac622b71?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/default-values-of-primitive-types-in-java-1toszbks0","summary":"Learn about the default values of primitive types in Java, which are important for understanding uninitialized variables and writing correct code.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/06dc7cd0cfcaa0457f79a5abbfd0ef67?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-02T14:07:13.990Z"},{"id":"F1X7M58Nr","title":"Interview Questions \u2014 Annotations in Java","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/interview-questions-annotations-in-java-3e91393282e?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/interview-questions-annotations-in-java-f1x7m58nr","summary":"Java annotations are metadata that provide additional information about code elements. They can be defined using the @interface keyword and used to configure code behavior. The @Override annotation is used to indicate a method override. Annotations can be processed at runtime using Java's Reflection API.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/06a1f68ca924aea8946112c654c2eb77?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":8,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-10-25T07:16:02.341Z"},{"id":"mIWkOtFeA","title":"Functional Interface Annotation in Java","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/functional-interface-annotation-in-java-2e04a1b58f0e?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/functional-interface-annotation-in-java-miwkotfea","summary":"Java introduced the FunctionalInterface annotation in Java 8 to designate an interface as a functional interface. Functional interfaces are interfaces in Java that have one abstract method and are essential for enabling lambda expressions and simplifying code. The @FunctionalInterface annotation acts as a marker interface and provides documentation to maintain the functional nature of an interface. It is important to use the @FunctionalInterface annotation when creating custom functional interfaces, to communicate intent clearly to other developers, and to encourage the use of lambda expressions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9af9d2676b7889544f6079d4d0ff0721?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-23T07:02:44.249Z"},{"id":"LJu0Or8ug","title":"Runnable vs Callable in Java","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/runnable-vs-callable-in-java-5cb9de757b16?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/runnable-vs-callable-in-java-lju0or8ug","summary":"Java has two main interfaces for defining concurrent tasks: Runnable and Callable. Runnable is a simple way to create tasks that run independently, while Callable allows for more control and can return a result or throw an exception. Understanding the differences between the two is important for writing efficient multithreaded applications in Java.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d1efcf50c0d7a5d51360ed7deb1cb9b1?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-19T07:02:43.662Z"},{"id":"bXV8OhR05","title":"Complete Guide for Optional in Java","url":"https://medium.com/codimis/complete-guide-for-optional-in-java-4731087fe3a2?source=rss----fce07aa30ec0---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/complete-guide-for-optional-in-java-bxv8ohr05","summary":"A comprehensive guide on Optional in Java, including its purpose, creation methods, and methods to access the value. Optional helps handle null values and avoid NullPointerExceptions, providing a more structured and safer way to represent the absence of a value.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1bdf6b9500d6f5f4acff2a74eeeb5a54?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-16T07:29:18.360Z"}],"similar_handles":["tkdodo","exakat","csswe","robinwieruch","allaboutcoding"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"tkdodo","handle":"tkdodo","name":"TkDodo","is_squad":false,"x":-8.431,"y":7.1605,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":50,"image":"h